  "coding-04-expression-eval":{category:"coding",title:"Build an arithmetic expression evaluator with exact precedence, associativity, and error contracts",objective:[["obj-1","`node evaluator.js` runs without throwing and prints exactly 12 'INPUT => RESULT' lines in the order the vectors appear in the test file, with numeric results formatted via standard JS `String(x)` conversion"],["obj-2","Precedence/associativity vectors are all correct: `2+3*4` => 14, `(2+3)*4` => 20, `2^3^2` => 512, `\\\" 10 -  4-3 \\\"` (JS-literal form; spaces are part of the input) => 3, `100/5/2` => 10 (judge recomputes each independently; the whitespace vector also verifies the tokenizer handles irregular spacing)"],["obj-3","Unary-minus vectors are all correct: `-2^2` => -4, `6*-2` => -12, `-(3+4)^2` => -49, `4^-1` => 0.25"],["obj-4","Error vectors return the exact strings: `8/(3-3)` => 'ERROR: division by zero'; `2**3` and `(1+2` => 'ERROR: syntax' (byte-exact; judge verifies with a two-line node require snippet against `module.exports.evaluate`, confirming it returns the string rather than throwing)"],["obj-5","REASONING.md exists, is at most 300 words (whole file, `wc -w`), and names the parsing strategy used (e.g. recursive descent or shunting-yard)"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Parser correctness & robustness",0.4],["sub-craft","Implementation architecture",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.5,subjective:0.5}},
