  "reverse-02-capsule-log":{category:"reverse-engineering",title:"Decode the PLQ Sensor Capsule",objective:[["obj-1","decoded.json contains magic 'PLQ', version 2, station id exactly 769 (fails if 259, the big-endian misread), and record count 3"],["obj-2","Record 1: channel 17 (0x11) with readings exactly [42, 769, 4096]"],["obj-3","Record 2: channel 130 (0x82) with label exactly 'pump-4'; record 3: channel 7 with readings exactly [500, 5]"],["obj-4","REASONING.md (or decoded.json) identifies the undocumented trailing byte as the sum of that record's payload bytes mod 256 (a checksum), and reports all three trailing bytes as valid checksums: 0x3e (62) for record 1, 0x23 (35) for record 2, 0xfa (250) for record 3"],["obj-5","Judge runs decoder.js on the embedded 32-byte hex string — its output values match decoded.json (structure/key names may differ, but values must agree), and the decoder reports all 32 bytes consumed"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Clarity of the format write-up",0.4],["sub-craft","Decoder robustness",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
