  "reverse-06-cog-ladder":{category:"reverse-engineering",title:"Lift the Register Machine to Source",objective:[["obj-1","ANSWER.md names the computed function as factorial (n!), and states the seed accumulator is 1 (not 0)"],["obj-2","Judge runs `node lifted.js` and it prints factorial values for n=0,1,5,7,10 as exactly 1, 1, 120, 5040, 3628800"],["obj-3","lifted.js exports a function (via module.exports) that returns 3628800 for input 10 and 1 for input 0 when the judge calls it directly, AND auto-prints the reference vector only under require.main===module so both the direct-run and require paths work from one file"],["obj-4","ANSWER.md's step-count or trace shows the loop multiplies the accumulator by r0 BEFORE decrementing r0 and terminates via the JZ-on-r0 branch (not an off-by-one that skips the largest factor)"],["obj-5","lifted.js is a structured high-level reimplementation (a real loop or recursion), not a re-embedding of the bytecode array plus an interpreter tuned to echo the expected numbers"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Lift readability",0.4],["sub-craft","Equivalence rigor",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
