  "reverse-09-braid-mill":{category:"reverse-engineering",title:"Invert the Layered Encoding Pipeline",objective:[["obj-1","ANSWER.md names all three transforms — XOR-with-0x2A, whole-buffer byte-reversal, and base64 — and states that base64 is the outermost stage, so decoding undoes base64 FIRST, then the byte-reversal and the XOR (in either relative order); the answer must not omit the byte-reversal stage"],["obj-2","Judge runs `node invert.js` and it prints the recovered plaintext of the challenge blob \\\"GB5CSURPSA==\\\" as exactly \\\"bench42\\\""],["obj-3","invert.js correctly round-trips BOTH embedded examples: decoding \\\"Zm9uZWc=\\\" yields \\\"MODEL\\\" and decoding \\\"SUhL\\\" yields \\\"abc\\\""],["obj-4","ANSWER.md shows the intermediate bytes for at least one example (e.g. \\\"MODEL\\\": utf8 4d4f44454c, XORed 67656e6f66, reversed 666f6e6567, base64 Zm9uZWc=), demonstrating the byte-reversal stage is present and not skipped"],["obj-5","invert.js implements a generic staged decoder (applies base64-decode, byte-reverse, and XOR-0x2A to any input blob), not a lookup table mapping the given blobs to answers"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Pipeline exposition",0.4],["sub-craft","Inversion correctness",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
