  "sched-03-two-machine-makespan":{category:"temporal-scheduling",title:"Makespan under two-machine resource contention",objective:[["obj-1","The makespan is stated as exactly 18"],["obj-2","The assignment matches the deterministic rule: J1 m0 [0,5], J2 m1 [0,3], J4 m1 [3,5], J3 m0 [5,13], J5 m1 [5,11], J7 m1 [11,18], J6 m0 [13,17]"],["obj-3","Every job's start is >= the max finish of its predecessors (precedence respected, e.g. J6 starts at 13 = max(J3=13, J4=5))"],["obj-4","No two jobs on the same machine overlap in time (verifiable by scanning each machine's interval list)"],["obj-5","The submission's account of the assignment (in schedule.md or REASONING.md) reflects event-driven assignment honoring the priority list, not a duration-sorted (e.g. shortest-job-first) or unlimited-parallelism approach (prose-located)"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Correctness and completeness of the machine assignment and makespan",0.4],["sub-craft","Clarity of the step-by-step scheduler simulation trace",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
