  "sched-03c-towing-tank-runs":{category:"temporal-scheduling",title:"Makespan under two-towing-tank contention",objective:[["obj-1","The makespan is stated as exactly 23"],["obj-2","The assignment matches the deterministic rule: H1 t0 [0,6], H2 t1 [0,4], H4 t1 [4,7], H5 t1 [7,14], H3 t0 [6,16], H7 t1 [14,23], H6 t0 [16,22]"],["obj-3","Every run's start is >= the max finish of its prerequisite runs (dependency respected, e.g. H6 starts at 16 = max(H3=16, H4=7))"],["obj-4","No two runs on the same tank overlap in time (verifiable by scanning each tank's interval list)"],["obj-5","The submission's account of the assignment (in tow-schedule.md or REASONING.md) reflects event-driven assignment honoring the priority list, not a duration-sorted (e.g. shortest-run-first) or unlimited-parallelism approach (prose-located)"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Correctness and completeness of the machine assignment and makespan",0.4],["sub-craft","Clarity of the step-by-step scheduler simulation trace",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
  "sched-04-feasibility-or-proof":{category:"temporal-scheduling",title:"Feasibility — place every event or prove it cannot be done",objective:[["obj-1","Scenario S is declared SAT and the provided start times place each event fully within its window with no overlap (a valid example: A=0, B=2, C=5; judge accepts any non-overlapping assignment satisfying the windows)"],["obj-2","Scenario U is declared UNSAT"],["obj-3","The UNSAT justification states that all three U-events must lie within [0,6] (width 6) while total duration is 3+3+2=8 > 6 on a single room (prose-located)"],["obj-4","For Scenario S, the given assignment is checked to satisfy A in [0,3], B in [2,8], C in [5,9] with each start+duration <= its deadline and no pairwise overlap"],["obj-5","feasibility.md distinguishes the two verdicts and does not claim both instances are feasible or both infeasible (prose-located)"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Correctness of both verdicts and validity of the SAT assignment",0.4],["sub-craft","Rigor and clarity of the infeasibility (pigeonhole) argument",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
