  "security-01-guestbook-fix":{category:"cybersecurity",title:"Three flaws in the Harborlight Inn guest lookup",objective:[["obj-1","FINDINGS.md identifies all three seeded flaws (SQL injection via string concatenation, hardcoded admin secret compared with ==, Math.random session tokens), each with an approximately correct line reference; missing any one fails"],["obj-2","`node fixed.js --selftest` prints SELFTEST OK as its final line (judge runs this literally)"],["obj-3","fixed.js contains no concatenation or template-interpolation of the guest name into SQL text — the query passed to db.query must be a constant string containing a `?` placeholder, with the name passed via the params array"],["obj-4","Token generation in fixed.js uses the crypto module (randomBytes or randomUUID) and the string `Math.random` appears nowhere in fixed.js"],["obj-5","The literal string `harborlight-admin-2019` does not appear anywhere in fixed.js; the secret is read from configuration/environment instead"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Fix quality and behavior preservation",0.4],["sub-craft","Findings clarity and risk explanation",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.5,subjective:0.5}},
