  "sql-01-join-cardinality":{category:"sql-reasoning",title:"Order rollup across customers with and without orders",objective:[["obj-1","ANSWERS.md reports exactly 5 total customers and 3 customers with at least one order (COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id)); a submission answering 5/5 or 5/7 fails"],["obj-2","Per-customer order counts are exactly Ash=3, Bo=1, Cy=3, Di=0, El=0, with Di and El present showing 0 (not omitted and not 1); judge re-runs the submission's query in node:sqlite and matches the full 5-row set"],["obj-3","Per-customer total spend is exactly Ash=130, Cy=100, Bo=40, Di=0, El=0, with zero-order customers showing 0 (not NULL, not absent); judge re-runs in node:sqlite"],["obj-4","The order-count query (QUERIES.sql) uses a LEFT (or equivalent outer) JOIN and COUNT(o.id) / COALESCE rather than INNER JOIN or a bare COUNT(*) over the join, so that zero-order customers are structurally retained with count 0 — judge inspects the SQL text as well as re-executing it"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Correctness of join choice and null-safe counting",0.4],["sub-craft","SQL readability and result-set presentation",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.7,subjective:0.3}},
