  "writing-09-steelman-memo":{category:"writing",title:"\"Persuasive memo with a mandatory steelman\"",objective:[["obj-1","memo.md contains a clearly labeled steelman/opposing-view section presenting the case AGAINST the 4-day week, incorporating at least two of the three supplied concerns (client-coverage gaps, payroll-parity cost, onboarding drag), each stated as a genuine concern rather than dismissed (prose-located check; ships 2-3 PASS + 2-3 FAIL example phrasings)"],["obj-2","memo.md takes and argues the PRO position (adopt the 4-day work week) as its overall recommendation — the conclusion is unambiguous, not neutral (prose-located check; ships 2-3 PASS + 2-3 FAIL example phrasings)"],["obj-3","The misleading 40%-productivity statistic from the unrelated furniture-import firm is NOT used as supporting evidence: it is either omitted entirely or explicitly called out as non-comparable/irrelevant (prose-located check; ships 2-3 PASS + 2-3 FAIL example phrasings)"],["obj-4","memo.md is structured with all four required moves present, in a recognizable order: a recommendation, the steelman, a rebuttal/response to it, and a close"],["obj-5","memo.md whole-file word count is between 350 and 500 inclusive, verified with wc -w"]],subjective:[["sub-quality","Persuasive force and quality of the rebuttal",0.4],["sub-craft","Fairness of the steelman (opposing case stated at its genuine strongest)",0.3],["sub-reasoning","Reasoning quality",0.3]],weights:{objective:0.5,subjective:0.5}},
